    title: "The Warm Furrow"
    excerpt: "Dawn smelled of frost and wet fur. Boof put her nose to the ground. Beneath the berry rows, ants kept their little hearths. Their patient magic warmed the roots through winter. Above them, the boonberries slept under ..."
